<article class="env-definition" id="01OP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01OP">Definition <span data-tag="01OP">28.4.1</span>.</a> Let $P$ be a property of rings. We say that $P$ is <em>local</em> if the following hold: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
For any ring $R$, and any $f \in R$ we have $P(R) \Rightarrow P(R_ f)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For any ring $R$, and $f_ i \in R$ such that $(f_1, \ldots , f_ n) = R$ then $\forall i, P(R_{f_ i}) \Rightarrow P(R)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>